  <section class="training-answer-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">The conversation framework</div>
      <h2>The ANSWER Call Framework.</h2>
      <p class="training-section-intro">A cold call is not a speech. It is a sequence of decisions that earns enough attention for the buyer and seller to determine whether another conversation makes sense.</p>
      <div class="training-answer-rail" role="img" aria-label="CallTeam ANSWER Call Framework for SDR conversations">
        <article><b>A</b><small>ACCOUNT CONTEXT</small><strong>Know why this company belongs in the campaign.</strong></article>
        <article><b>N</b><small>NATURAL OPENING</small><strong>Sound composed, direct, and human from the first sentence.</strong></article>
        <article><b>S</b><small>SIGNAL AND RELEVANCE</small><strong>Connect the call to something the buyer can recognize.</strong></article>
        <article><b>W</b><small>WORDS BUYERS UNDERSTAND</small><strong>Remove internal language, clutter, and empty sales phrases.</strong></article>
        <article><b>E</b><small>EXPLORE THE RESPONSE</small><strong>Listen, ask, clarify, and understand what resistance means.</strong></article>
        <article><b>R</b><small>ROUTE THE NEXT STEP</small><strong>Qualify whether another conversation deserves to happen.</strong></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

